{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "06TD", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-minimality}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b75cb29cb1f65ad4d3c2cd675800e38b1454abcb8ba5333edd8010a52b1ac16d", "source_text": "Remarks regarding minimality", "source_text_hash": "sha256:59fa54ae28d24047e2263aaaf6b4fd2ceb2aa8c84ae118c081af3d6486a47ecb", "unit_id": "tag:06TD:title"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06TD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-presentation-deformation-groupoid}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{section-minimal-versal}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{section-miniversal-objects-existence}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fb6ad280346362a580dd3b1ba5464da5eea3146f40ecf0a8f3a682476d6fa006", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ec3dcefe330057fe28b171f4532ff35bd0f95449680aff9230fa2142c1c85950", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe main theorem of this chapter is\nTheorem <REF_0001>\nabove. It describes completely those categories cofibred in groupoids\nover <MATH_0001> which have a presentation by a\nsmooth prorepresentable groupoid in functors. In this section we briefly\ndiscuss how the minimality discussed in\nSections <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>\ncan be used to obtain a ``minimal'' smooth prorepresentable presentation.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2206f71c809f64291427f9c0988db4ba9684d24091b31db2ad6ef3f4f415cf37", "unit_id": "tag:06TD:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06TD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0004": "$(U(k[\\epsilon]), R(k[\\epsilon]), s, t, c)$", "MATH_0005": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to [U/R]$", "MATH_0007": "$[U/R]$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-minimal-groupoid-in-functors}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2d963953d90c3bf9040e2a2f7ea768b1db9785b109e03f91b8ca61ad13c82d1e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:422bed1d460b108363d889d0b8e63a03c6ca1e22ab7b63e06ddd253274dee49c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a smooth prorepresentable groupoid in functors\non <MATH_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> We say <MATH_0003> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>normalized<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if the groupoid\n<MATH_0004> is totally disconnected,\ni.e., there are no morphisms between distinct objects.\n<STRUCT_0003> We say <MATH_0005> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>minimal<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if the <MATH_0006>\nis given by a minimal versal formal object of <MATH_0007>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fc2d43ce6c52d19e0b4cbe2b24990ab5c5832840cea948c5b302c975741e72e3", "unit_id": "tag:06KM:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06TD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$k' \\subset k$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-bijective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{equation-bijective-orbits}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d012609d04f3650f5a5489156f4762b92df28b31e6d2d64b6a21fe125d6164a0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4aea7f985923851a3ce4eaa8070a4ace39009a286d586c390f0411decff3dbd7", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe difference between the two notions is related to the difference between\nconditions (<REF_0001>) and (<REF_0002>)\nand disappears when <MATH_0001> is separable. Also a\nnormalized smooth prorepresentable groupoid in functors is minimal\nas the following lemma shows. Here is a precise statement.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9e12a1b7f2547eb3920e956e23ad41155a7acece1d3010d34e514a42785507ff", "unit_id": "tag:06TD:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06TD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to [U/R]$", "MATH_0005": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0006": "$TU \\to T[U/R]$", "MATH_0007": "$\\text{Der}_\\Lambda(k, k) \\to TU$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-minimal-groupoid-in-functors}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ccbee746606de860aff75be07d1ad361169dbceaf077bd6d5b0d74d3c9cecf0a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:154ab98e815f17fc6b5e1e11437559eac409b37773400593e4f109cd42530380", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a smooth prorepresentable groupoid in\nfunctors on <MATH_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> is normalized if and only if the morphism\n<MATH_0004> induces an isomorphism on tangent spaces, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is minimal if and only if the kernel of\n<MATH_0006> is contained in the image of\n<MATH_0007>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3f9b6975d54bee888240986feafdc1a9bab40b26de38bec09ab8bb4837b7aae5", "unit_id": "tag:06KN:statement"}
